WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:04.514
In this video tutorial, I'm going
to be showing you how to connect

00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:09.384
Claude to Blender to have Claude
help you build things within Blender.

00:00:09.514 --> 00:00:11.693
First things first, make
sure you are running the most

00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:13.443
up-to-date version of Blender.

00:00:13.443 --> 00:00:16.743
You can open the Blender app,
go into the settings here, go to

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.884
About Blender, and it will tell
you what version you are running.

00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:24.403
This will work on any version
of Blender, whatever operating

00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:26.093
system that you are using.

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:31.073
You wanna start over in Claude, and
once you're here, I want you to go up

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:36.163
to Claude in the settings and go to
the option here that says Connectors.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:40.033
Under Customize, it says Connectors,
and this is where we will add the

00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:43.284
connection from Claude over to Blender.

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:47.314
So go ahead and go to Connectors
here under Settings, go to Add,

00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:49.044
and then go to Browse Connectors.

00:00:49.284 --> 00:00:52.833
Then type in the search box
and type in the word Blender.

00:00:53.034 --> 00:00:57.583
You should see the Blender logo here,
and then click the addition symbol

00:00:57.583 --> 00:01:00.103
to add that, and then go to Install.

00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:03.613
Once you've installed it, you may
have to click Install one more time

00:01:03.613 --> 00:01:08.363
for confirmation, and you'll see the
process here with a little progress bar.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:12.303
Once it is installed, I want you
to click the link button right here

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:14.014
next to the Install button there.

00:01:14.014 --> 00:01:18.043
Make sure that shows as a check mark,
and then go ahead and make sure it

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.843
is enabled and over to the right.

00:01:20.053 --> 00:01:24.933
Then you can click on Configure to see all
of the different things and abilities that

00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:27.973
Blender has and how you want it to work.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:32.164
If you click the hand icon next
to a permission, that means that

00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:36.234
it has to ask you first before
it goes and does the action.

00:01:36.424 --> 00:01:40.244
If you have this set to a check mark
like this one here, Get Blend File

00:01:40.253 --> 00:01:44.753
Data Block Summary, this means that
it will always allow it automatically.

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:49.673
Just to be safe, you may wanna just
select the hand icon here to bring up

00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:53.303
that prompt to say, "Hey, I want to
allow it to do this," so it doesn't

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:57.433
mess up a project that you've already
been working on for hours at a time.

00:01:57.813 --> 00:02:00.983
The next thing you wanna do is
open up a new browser tab or Google

00:02:00.983 --> 00:02:03.613
and go and search for Blender MCP.

00:02:03.753 --> 00:02:07.783
Once you've done that, you'll see the
top option that says MCP Server, and

00:02:07.784 --> 00:02:09.903
it'll have the Blender icon or logo.

00:02:10.144 --> 00:02:11.054
Click onto that.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.263
Then I want you to scroll down to where
you see the section that says Add-on.

00:02:15.926 --> 00:02:19.716
I want you to go and download
this add-on, so click Download.

00:02:19.746 --> 00:02:21.676
You'll see it here in Chrome.

00:02:21.706 --> 00:02:23.176
It shows as a download.

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:24.236
Do not open it.

00:02:24.256 --> 00:02:26.465
What I want you to do
is find that download.

00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:27.616
Don't extract it.

00:02:27.626 --> 00:02:28.406
Don't open it.

00:02:28.445 --> 00:02:31.585
I want you to click and hold
and drag that into Blender.

00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:37.896
When you do so, you will see this box
here, Install from Disk, User Default.

00:02:38.136 --> 00:02:39.766
Go ahead and click OK.

00:02:40.236 --> 00:02:43.986
To confirm in Blender that you've
done everything correctly, go to

00:02:43.986 --> 00:02:48.345
the Edit option in the menu bar
like so, and go to Preferences.

00:02:48.755 --> 00:02:52.896
Once here, under Preferences, I want
you to go to Add-ons, and then under the

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:58.156
Search Add-on box here, type in MCP, and
you should see where it says MCP, and

00:02:58.156 --> 00:02:59.925
there should be a check mark next to it.

00:03:00.095 --> 00:03:04.115
At this point, if you don't see it or
it's not working, make sure the box is

00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:06.485
checked, and then just drag it once more.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:09.185
Sometimes you have to drag
it twice or even three times

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.775
to get it to work properly.

00:03:10.925 --> 00:03:13.755
Just follow the previous steps
and you should be good to go.

00:03:14.075 --> 00:03:17.275
All right, now let's test and
make sure everything is working.

00:03:17.275 --> 00:03:19.705
As you can see on the left
here, we have Blender.

00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:21.036
On the right, we have Claude.

00:03:21.235 --> 00:03:23.845
The first thing I'm gonna do is ask
it, are you connected to Blender?

00:03:24.295 --> 00:03:27.956
Something else you may have to do once
you've asked it, is it connected to

00:03:27.956 --> 00:03:30.025
Blender, is actually start the server.

00:03:30.025 --> 00:03:32.935
It may give you this when you ask
it, are you connected to Blender.

00:03:33.115 --> 00:03:38.325
You go back to Preferences, Add-ons,
search for MCP, and then expand the option

00:03:38.335 --> 00:03:41.435
here and go to Start MCP Bridge Server.

00:03:41.685 --> 00:03:45.615
And then as you can see, it says online
access must be enabled in the System

00:03:45.615 --> 00:03:51.204
Preferences And then what you want to do
is go to Edit, and then go to Preferences,

00:03:51.244 --> 00:03:55.924
and then under System here where it
says Network, go to Allow Online Access.

00:03:56.184 --> 00:04:01.323
Then you go back to add-ons, search
for MCP, and go to Start MCP Bridge

00:04:01.323 --> 00:04:03.313
Server, and you should be good to go.

00:04:03.613 --> 00:04:06.924
Now I've asked Claude again, "Are
you connected to Blender?" after

00:04:06.924 --> 00:04:10.464
doing those things, and it should
say, "Yes, I'm connected." As you

00:04:10.464 --> 00:04:12.393
can see, yes, I'm connected now.

00:04:12.683 --> 00:04:16.243
Then I'm just going to ask it to
create me a simple house structure

00:04:16.253 --> 00:04:20.603
in my current open project in
Blender just to show how this works.

00:04:20.973 --> 00:04:24.233
As with everything as we've set up with
the Blender connection, I'll have to

00:04:24.254 --> 00:04:28.574
allow it to have access to certain areas
of Blender, so I'm gonna do that now.

00:04:28.824 --> 00:04:31.684
Then it starts asking me questions
like, "How detailed should the house

00:04:31.684 --> 00:04:34.714
be?" Um, let's do basic block and roof.

00:04:34.754 --> 00:04:36.823
And then, "What should I
do with the default cube?"

00:04:36.874 --> 00:04:37.873
Go ahead and delete it.

00:04:37.903 --> 00:04:40.593
So it's asking me questions
about the project already.

00:04:40.973 --> 00:04:44.443
And now you can see here over in Blender
it has created that house structure.

00:04:44.504 --> 00:04:48.434
As we've discussed within Claude,
it can be as detailed or simple

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:52.023
as you want, but the power in this
is the back and forth with Claude.

00:04:52.313 --> 00:04:57.103
So I can go back and forth with Claude
after it gives me the initial object and

00:04:57.103 --> 00:05:01.143
say, "No, I want the roof bigger," or,
"No, I want it to be this shape," or,

00:05:01.144 --> 00:05:02.694
"I want the color to be this," right?

00:05:02.824 --> 00:05:05.243
It then gives me a recap
of what it's done, right?

00:05:05.324 --> 00:05:07.123
It says, "Okay, I built the new house.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.683
Here's exactly the details of it." And it
says, "One note, do you want me to add a

00:05:10.684 --> 00:05:14.133
door, windows, and materials next?" And
you just go back and forth with Claude

00:05:14.403 --> 00:05:16.243
until you get the result that you want.

00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:19.744
If you have any questions, I'll put some
frequently asked questions down below.

00:05:19.903 --> 00:05:22.083
And with that said, I'll
see you in the next video.

